  Well, yes, but if they accidently hit another monster while confused, the
other monster doesn't get mad.  If YOU accidently his a peaceful monster,
the peaceful monster will then become highly upset, and try to eat your face
off.
  As someone else mentioned, it wouldn't really do to have this happen all
the time.  If an elf accidently runs his pal through with a sword, the other
elf might understand, seeing as elf #1 was confused and it was an accident
and all.  If elf #1 get confused and swipes at, oh, say, a dwarf, I would
think the dwarf would attack the elf, as he would attack you, if YOU had
accidently hit him.
  I'm not sure what all the fields are in monster attributes, and maybe this
would mean adding a whole other field to the description, but maybe if they
could add just one field that indicated "Peaceful" or "Hostile".  Peaceful
creatures, when accidently attacked by members of their own type ignore the
attack, as all monsters currently do.  Hostile creatures, orcs and ogres and
unruly things like that, when accidently attacked by members of their own
type would attack the unfortunate creature who accidently hit them.  At any
rate, any creature hit by any other creature of a different type, would
immedinately yell "TRAITOR!" and turn to fight.
  Scenerio example:
  Bob, our player, is being attacked.  Theres a dwarf in hand to hand
combat, Orc #1 right behind him, and Orc #2 behind Orc #1.
  Orc #2 cleverly fires a wand of magic missile at the player.  Orc #1 and
the dwarf are both hit.
  Orc #1, being an Orc, a very nasty sort of creature who only hangs around
other Orcs because he hopes the others will die so he doesn't have to,
becomes highly irrate at Orc #2, and attacks him.
  The dwarf, who never really liked Orcs to begin with, also turns to try
and attack Orc #2.
  The dwarf, who also has a wand of magic-missile, fireas at Orc #2, hitting
Orc #1 in the process.  Orc #1 now becomes angry at the dwarf, and turns to
fight HIM.

  So, we have Bob, who quietly sneaks off, while the dwarf is fighting Orc
#1, who is under attack by Orc #2 (who was angered after Orc #1 attacked
him, after he (Orc #2) hit him (Orc #1) with the magic missile).

  See?  Simple!  :)  The way some monsters sling arrows and fire wands in a
haphazard manner (with regard to his friends and fellow monsters), every now
and then an enormous brawl would break out among the creatures, while the
player stands there yelling "Hey!  HEY!  What about MEEEEeeeEEEE???"

  Alternative #1:
  Creatures already in combat with the player would not cease in order to
attack another monster.  Thus, in the above scenerio, Orcs #1 and #2 would
be having a serious knock-down-drag-out fight while Bob and the dwarf
continue their fight.

I think that would just be terribly ammusing, AND it would be consistant with
the way it already works:  if peaceful creatures get mad at the player for
an accidental hit, they should get mad any anyone who hits them by accident.

(Maybe beef up the code so monsters actually look to see where they're
shooting before they shoot, so an orc at the end of a line doesn't waste the
whole troop with a wand of death...  Much...)

  Additional Feature #1:
  Creatures who fight each other due to a Ring of Conflict wouldn't hold any
grudges against each other if the ring is taken off.  They would all know
it's not the fault of the creature that was trying to kill them.  It was....
"THE PLAYER!" they all yell simultaniously, right before they yell "LET'S
GET HIM!", right after the nymph ran off with that ring...

